From 34f6f23a25c3d18486d8d778eea28364a7532906 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 02:42:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] db: hold pools behind interfaces that name no pgxpool type

*pgxpool.Pool holds puddle's generic pool and *pgxpool.Conn its generic
resource. DB held a *pgxpool.Pool and named both types in its method
signatures, so every package that could see a *keel.DB compiled 93 of
puddle's functions again (about 24 KB and 0.1 s each).

DB and its replicas now hold their pools as connPool and acquired
connections as poolConn, interfaces whose methods name no pgxpool type
beyond the non-generic Stat and Config. DB.Pool becomes the function
keel.Pool(db), and DB.Stat returns the primary pool's statistics, so
only a caller of keel.Pool compiles puddle.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G7VRX61CtQMdWhsgQH4ew6
